---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The rules for using the NeuroGIDAS website, a student-run club site at Eastview High School."
  updated="October 20, 2026"
  summary={[
    'This is a student club’s website. It is not an official Eastview High School or District 196 site.',
    'Everything here is for general information and learning. It is not medical advice.',
    'Meeting dates and topics can change. Check the GroupMe for the latest.',
    'You can share links to the site, but please don’t copy our logo, photos, or text as your own.',
    'Other websites we link to have their own rules.',
  ]}
>
  <h2>Using this site</h2>
  <p>
    By using neurogidas-web.vercel.app, you agree to these terms. If you don’t agree, please don’t use the site. These terms
    apply to everyone who visits, whether or not you are a club member.
  </p>

  <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
  <p>
    NeuroGIDAS is run by students at Eastview High School. It is a student-led group, and its views are not necessarily those of
    Eastview High School or Independent School District 196. Nothing on this site is an official statement from the school or the
    district. GIDAS is the high school program of miRcore, and this site is not run by miRcore.
  </p>

  <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
  <p>
    The site talks about the brain, genes, and diseases so students can learn about them. None of it is medical advice, and it
    should not be used to diagnose or treat anyone. If you have a health question, talk to a doctor or another qualified
    professional.
  </p>

  <h2>Schedules and events</h2>
